// A product is not a number. `{x: 1} * {x: 2}` type-checks (arithmetic
// unifies its operands) and, until 2026-09-27, emitted i32.mul over the two
// record ADDRESSES with zero diagnostics — measured on boot 5bf55b68:
// compiled, then TRAPPED at run time reading a field off the product of two
// addresses (exit 134). Arithmetic now DEMANDS a number of its operand at
// the judgment (infer.mn numeric_demand): the operand is bound to a record
// when `*` is judged, so the refusal lands at the operator, `mentl check`
// says so, and no WAT streams (E_ArithOnAggregate, armed at birth;
// Hβ.emit.arith-on-aggregate-is-pointer-arith).
fn main() = {
  let p = {x: 1} * {x: 2}
  p.x
}
